+// FIX: Hub Performance (map, list, leaderboard, today chart, remarks log,
+// trend report, and CSV export) used to read `issue.hub` directly instead of
+// going through getIssueHubName(). That meant a manually-set/overridden Hub
+// Name (from the Hub Info modal, e.g. when the sheet lookup missed or got a
+// ticket's hub wrong) showed correctly in the Issue Tracker table and its
+// Hub Name filter, but the SAME ticket was still grouped under its old
+// auto-fetched hub (or dumped into "Unassigned" if none was ever fetched)
+// everywhere in Hub Performance — silently splitting one hub's numbers
+// across two buckets. Every hub-grouping function below now calls this
+// single helper so "manual overrides win, else auto-fetched, else
+// Unassigned" is applied exactly once and stays consistent everywhere.
+function getIssueHubNameOrUnassigned(issue) {
+    const name = getIssueHubName(issue);
+    return name ? name : 'Unassigned';
+}
